WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.551
Sammy was a cute sparrow.

2
00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:12.509
He flew over the river with his mom.

3
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:17.334
"Oh, Mom, it's cloudy today," Sammy said.

4
00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:21.553
"Yes, Sammy," said Mom.

5
00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:25.510
"It looks like it will rain soon."

6
00:00:25.511 --> 00:00:29.425
"Mom, I'm hungry," Sammy complained.

7
00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:32.092
"Yes, I'm also hungry.

8
00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:35.341
Let's find something to eat."

9
00:00:35.342 --> 00:00:38.277
"Mom, Mom!" Sammy said.

10
00:00:38.278 --> 00:00:39.872
"Rest in the woods.

11
00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.671
I will go and get some food."

12
00:00:42.672 --> 00:00:46.507
"Can you do it by yourself?" Mom asked.

13
00:00:46.508 --> 00:00:54.702
"Sure, I can!" Sammy was old enough to find food on his own.

14
00:00:54.703 --> 00:00:57.847
He was a good flier too.

15
00:00:57.848 --> 00:01:01.916
He flew around the river to look for insects.

16
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:05.138
But he couldn't find a single one.

17
00:01:05.139 --> 00:01:07.694
"Hmm, this is strange.

18
00:01:07.695 --> 00:01:12.117
Why can't I find any insects?" he wondered.

19
00:01:12.118 --> 00:01:16.318
Sammy felt tired and went back to his mom.

20
00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:21.329
"Mom, I searched hard, but I couldn't find a single insect.

21
00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:25.969
I used to see insects everywhere, but now they are gone."

22
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:31.197
"Sammy, why don't you fly low?" Mom suggested.

23
00:01:31.198 --> 00:01:35.710
"What? You want me to fly low?" Sammy asked.

24
00:01:35.711 --> 00:01:38.435
"Yes, fly low.

25
00:01:38.436 --> 00:01:42.403
Then you will see the insects."

26
00:01:42.404 --> 00:01:46.604
Sammy took his mom's advice.

27
00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:49.165
He flew around the river again.

28
00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:52.488
This time he flew low.

29
00:01:52.489 --> 00:01:58.229
"Wow! I couldn't find a single one when I flew high," he said.

30
00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:03.827
"Now I can see many insects. Yay!"

31
00:02:03.828 --> 00:02:12.078
Sammy caught a big insect and brought it to his mom.

32
00:02:12.079 --> 00:02:15.112
"Mom, I don't understand.

33
00:02:15.113 --> 00:02:18.673
Why are all the insects so close to the ground?"

34
00:02:18.674 --> 00:02:21.025
His mother explained.

35
00:02:21.026 --> 00:02:24.913
"Before it rains, the air gets moist.

36
00:02:24.914 --> 00:02:29.484
The moisture in the air makes insects' wings heavy.

37
00:02:29.485 --> 00:02:34.865
So the insects fly in the grass and bushes near the ground."

38
00:02:34.866 --> 00:02:38.679
Sammy understood. "I get it!

39
00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.489
So when it looks like it will rain, I should fly low to look for insects."

40
00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:46.711
"Right!" said Mom.

41
00:02:46.712 --> 00:02:50.375
Just then it started to rain.

42
00:02:50.376 --> 00:02:59.906
Sammy and his mom watched the raindrops and smiled.

